---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getApp, COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('workshop')!;
const lastUpdated = 'August 10, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${app.name} Privacy Policy — ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description={`How ${app.name} collects, uses, and protects your information.`}
  path={`/${app.slug}/privacy`}
  noindex={true}
>
  <article class="prose container">
    <a class="back-link" href="/workshop">← {app.name}</a>
    <h1>{app.name} Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how {COMPANY.name} (“we”, “us”) handles
      information in connection with the {app.name} iPhone and iPad app,
      website, and related server features (the “Service”). Workshop is a
      single-user woodworking project companion. We collect only the
      information needed to provide, secure, and support it.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account information.</strong> You may sign in with Apple or
        Microsoft. We receive a stable account identifier and the basic profile
        information the provider makes available, such as your name and email
        address. Apple may provide a private relay address instead of your
        personal email. For Apple accounts, our server also receives the
        one-time authorization code and securely stores an encrypted revocation
        credential so it can revoke access if you delete your account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Workshop data you create.</strong> Content you generate in the
        app — such as projects, Shaper projects, templates, cut lists, stock and
        material data, shopping lists, build logs, finish records, notes,
        instructions, costs, and progress photos — so the Service can plan your
        cuts and keep your project history.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Imported project data.</strong> When you paste a project link
        or ask Workshop to analyze one, we process the URL and referenced
        project content to extract parts, dimensions, and related build details
        into an editable draft in your account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Limited technical data.</strong> We process basic operational
        logs, such as request timestamps and error information, as needed to
        run, secure, and troubleshoot the Service.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do <strong>not</strong> collect precise location, contacts, or
      advertising identifiers. Workshop contains no third-party advertising and
      does not track you across other companies’ apps or websites.
    </p>

    <h2>Device permissions and local processing</h2>
    <p>
      Workshop asks for camera or photo access only when you choose to attach an
      image, scan a dimension, or select a photo through a system picker. Live
      Text dimension recognition runs on your device. A photo or Journaling
      Suggestion is uploaded only after you explicitly select it for a project.
      Notification permission is used for finish reminders and active cut or
      shopping sessions. App preferences, authentication credentials, and
      widget or Live Activity snapshots are stored in protected app, Keychain,
      or App Group storage on your device as appropriate.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide, maintain, and secure your account and the Service.</li>
      <li>
        To generate cut plans, save your projects and build logs, and track your
        progress.
      </li>
      <li>
        To import or analyze a project only when you ask the Service to do so.
      </li>
      <li>To diagnose problems and improve reliability and performance.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How your information is stored and protected</h2>
    <p>
      Your account data is isolated in a private, per-user SQLite database, with
      project images stored as account data or account-scoped uploads.
      Information is encrypted in transit using HTTPS. Authentication
      credentials are stored using platform security controls and, where stored
      by our server, encrypted at rest. The Service is hosted on Microsoft
      Azure, and access is limited to what is necessary to operate and secure
      it.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information. Information is processed by
      Microsoft Azure as our hosting provider, by Apple or Microsoft when you
      choose that company for authentication, and by our hosted project-analysis
      service only when you request an analysis. These providers process
      information only as needed to deliver their part of the Service. We may
      also disclose information where required by law or to protect the security
      of the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      We retain your Workshop information while your account is active. You can
      permanently delete the account from inside the iPhone or iPad app.
      Deletion removes the account’s projects, Shaper projects, templates, cut
      and material data, shopping lists, images, build and finish records,
      profile, and authentication state from Workshop. For an Apple account,
      Workshop revokes its stored Apple credential before removing local
      account data. For a Microsoft account, deletion removes only Workshop
      data; it does not delete your Microsoft account or revoke unrelated
      Microsoft access.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can export a JSON summary of your project list before deletion. This
      summary is a reference export, not a complete backup of project details or
      images. You may also request help with access or deletion by emailing
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is intended for a general, adult audience and is not directed
      to children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
      children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be
      reflected by updating the “Last updated” date above.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
